        "type": "text/html",
        "value": "<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><em>You&#x2019;re reading the web edition of D.C. Diagnosis, STAT&#x2019;s twice-weekly newsletter about the politics and policy of health and medicine.&#xa0;<a href=\"https://www.statnews.com/signup/dc/\">Sign up here</a>&#xa0;to receive it in your inbox on Tuesdays and Thursdays.</em></p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">House Republicans cancelled Friday&#x2019;s votes, which my colleague Chelsea Cirruzzo jokingly called the &#x201c;<a href=\"https://www.rockstargames.com/VI\">GTA 6</a> effect,&#x201d; much to my total confusion. Send news tips and &#x201c;single-player, third-person, action-adventure, open-world, sandbox video games&#x201d; to <a href=\"mailto:John.Wilkerson@statnews.com\">John.Wilkerson@statnews.com</a> or John_Wilkerson.07 on Signal.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"h-maha-pac-spends-on-itself\"><strong>MAHA PAC spends on itself</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">MAHA PAC leaders blamed the election losses of the movement&#x2019;s preferred candidates on the powerful forces supporting their rivals.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.statnews.com/2026/11/19/maha-pac-midterm-election-spending-fda-questions-after-heidi-overton/?utm_campaign=rss\">Continue to STAT+ to read the full story&hellip;</a></p>"
      }
